  "$comment": "Every pairing the contrast audit must verify, for both presets and for any saved custom theme. Thresholds are WCAG 2.1 AA: 4.5:1 for body text, 3:1 for large text, and 3:1 under 1.4.11 for anything that identifies a component boundary or state. Purely decorative dividers between surfaces carry no WCAG requirement and are not audited; anything that communicates a boundary or a state uses border-input or border-strong, which are. The rail's separation from the header is a design-quality concern rather than an accessibility one, and border-rail guarantees it, so it is not audited here.",
